module test.claim.long.emitted_lib_rs_module_declaration_witness_test

// Permanent regression control for the emitted `lib.rs` module list.
//
// THE DEFECT, now repaired: v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_lib_rs_from_files derived
// its module declarations from the files this emit actually produced, and then
// appended `pub mod v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated;` UNCONDITIONALLY from a
// hand-authored string. For the stage0 crate that module is real — a different
// emitter co-produces it — so the seed compiled and the fork stayed invisible.
// Every OTHER emitted crate got a declaration for a module nobody materialized,
// which rustc answers with E0583 and cargo with a failed build.
//
// WHERE IT SURFACED: the falsifier's wet lane. namespace_import_closure_receipt
// and self_host_logic_behavioral_receipt each emit a crate whose lib.rs is about
// a dozen lines; both died on `error[E0583]: file not found for module
// v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated` before reaching the behaviour they exist to
// measure, so two witnesses reported false for a reason unrelated to their subject.
//
// WHY A CONTROL RATHER THAN A LIST ENTRY: the declared set and the materialized
// set were two representations of one fact, and the hand-authored half could not
// be falsified by editing the derived half. Adding the missing file to a list
// would have greened this crate and preserved the class. The declaration now
// derives from the emitted file set, so a crate that did not produce the module
// cannot declare it.
//
// The required half is the non-vacuity half: it proves the oracle is reading a
// real lib.rs that declares this probe's own module, so the exclusion is
// evidence of absence rather than evidence of an unread file.
//
// THOSE TWO FACTS WERE TWO CLAIMS OVER ONE SOURCE UNTIL 2026-08-19, and that cost
// two full frontend-and-emitter crossings for one emitted lib.rs. They are one
// call now — a required token and a forbidden token over the same emitted file —
// because compile_dag_rust_emit_check already expresses exactly that conjunction,
// and because the non-vacuity argument above is precisely the claim that the two
// halves must be read off ONE emission. Neither assertion changed. The ordering
// probe below emits a genuinely different crate, so it stays a crossing of its own.
//
// THE SECOND DIMENSION, ORDER, is covered below, and the first revision of this
// file was wrong about who covered it: it deferred the ordering constraint to the
// stage0 regen drift gate. Stage0 takes the OTHER branch — it has compiler tests,
// so it calls order_lib_rs_mod_names and gets the dispatch declaration from the
// admitted hand block — so that gate never reaches the partial-crate ordering at
// all, and order_partial_lib_rs_mod_names could have been replaced by the identity
// function with every check in this repository still green. The claim was caught by
// review (gunbc#8222), not by execution, which is the point: a deferral naming the
// wrong consumer reads exactly like coverage.
//
// The ordering probe below therefore emits a crate that GENUINELY materializes the
// macro provider, so the provider partition is non-empty. Position is expressible in
// a substring oracle by anchoring: the emitted preamble is fixed, so pinning the
// provider declaration to the text immediately following it asserts the provider is
// the FIRST declaration, which membership alone cannot say.
//
// The anchor is the preamble rather than a neighbouring module because an adjacency
// oracle over the provider and the imported std module was written first, run, and
// REFUTED — other modules of the closure sit between them.
//
// DISCRIMINATION, measured rather than argued (this worktree, release claim_batch):
// with order_partial_lib_rs_mod_names as written the claim PASSES; with that function
// replaced by the identity, rebuilt, it FAILS. Raw emitted-file order does not put the
// provider first, so this claim is the control the ordering construction lacked.

data lrd_probe_source: String = "module lrd_probe\n\nimport std.types { Bool }\n\nfn lrd_true() -> Bool {\n  true\n}\n"

fn w_small_crate_lib_rs_omits_dispatch_and_declares_its_own_module() -> Bool {
  compile_dag_rust_emit_check(
    lrd_probe_source,
    "src/lib.rs",
    ["pub mod lrd_probe;"],
    ["v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated"]
  )
}

data lrd_provider_source: String = "module v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated\n\nimport std.types { Bool }\n\nfn lrd_provider_true() -> Bool {\n  true\n}\n"

fn w_partial_crate_declares_macro_provider_before_ordinary_modules() -> Bool {
  compile_dag_rust_emit_check(
    lrd_provider_source,
    "src/lib.rs",
    ["use im::\{OrdSet as BTreeSet, Vector as Vec};\n\n#[macro_use]\npub mod v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated;\n"],
    []
  )
}

test fn small_crate_lib_rs_omits_dispatch_and_declares_its_own_module() -> Bool {
  w_small_crate_lib_rs_omits_dispatch_and_declares_its_own_module()
}

test fn partial_crate_declares_macro_provider_before_ordinary_modules() -> Bool {
  w_partial_crate_declares_macro_provider_before_ordinary_modules()
}
